      "side": 1,
      "message": "So the use of SKU IDs to define configuration is deprecated, and instead the fw_config fields are to be used instead, similar to how it was done with the barrel-jack.\nThe idea is to define a field in the fw_config that provides a value that can be used to identify which thermal table should be used.\nThe default value of 0 should represent what the existing platforms expect.\nThe size of the field should be enough to cater for future values.\nSo it appears as though at least a 1 bit field should be used.\nI would allocate at least 2-3 bits for future expansion (4-8 possible thermal tables).",
